From ffd8ab1f001413dc836334a0758e951a31bf3a91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:02:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08094/11362] [outer-loop] HUD-mask review: positive morphology
 evidence, two mask defects, and the p-value the re-score should stop quoting

Applies the VERIFIED findings of an adversarial review of the two 2026-08-01 HUD
artifacts. Every claim was recomputed from the runs' own data first; two of the
review's figures did not reproduce as stated and are corrected rather than adopted.
No mask, threshold, score or verdict changed -- this adds evidence and names defects.

CAPTURE (results/arc_hud_mask_capture_20260801/):
- morphology_check.py + .json: POSITIVE evidence the bands are progress bars, from
  shape alone (two colours, single contiguous run, constant divider, mover-free,
  click-free, empties at level-up). 4 of 6 pass all five strictly; 5 of 6 once ka59's
  divider is read as "redraws only when the bar resets" -- it changes at exactly the
  transition the bar empties. The review said 5 of 6 pass strictly; that is corrected.
- ls20 masks HALF a two-row widget: rows 61/62 are byte-identical in 14/14 frames with
  identical change masks in 13/13 transitions. detect_hud_registers(edge_margin=2)
  cannot propose row 61 on a 64-row grid, so any HUD deeper than two cells is silently
  half-masked and the detector cannot report the shortfall. Not verdict-changing (a
  two-row mask overlaps 0.021 of changed cells, 24x under the swallow threshold).
- ls20 also FAILS the bar morphology outright (5 colours, no contiguous run). Three
  independent signals single out the same band.
- ka59 is the thinnest stage-1 defence: P1 failed (0.636 < 0.7), it ships on P2 alone
  with two action ids at n=4. Morphology, not the discriminators, carries it.
- NEW defect the review missed: alarm A1 is VACUOUS on ar25/ls20/tu93, whose routes
  contain no clicks at all. Three of six A1 passes carry no information.

RE-SCORE (results/arc_hud_masked_rescore_20260801/):
- harness/review_verification.py + review_verification.json: the mask deleted 27
  correctly-predicted cells against 491 spurious (5.2%); in 4 cells it removed ONLY
  correct ones and 3 of those scored HIGHER. 22 of 24 moving cells rose (p=3.6e-05),
  and the rise tracks baseline fidelity (r=+0.45), not spurious cells removed
  (r=-0.05) -- masking flatters whichever arm was ahead.
- 78.1% of the mask's aggregate benefit is s5i5 alone, whose tie was manufactured by
  deleting that engine's only three correct cells.
- AND THAT DESTROYED NEGATIVE WAS ITSELF AT THE A/A FLOOR, which neither the artifact
  nor the review said: the upstream A/A control re-ran the same arm at the same seed
  and got a different engine scoring 0.0 -- divergence 0.090909, the control's maximum
  and exactly the number at stake. So the masked p=0.0075 must not be quoted at all;
  use the mean (+0.0019 shift, ties kept). The conclusion is unchanged.

Both artifacts: adversarial_verify 0-flagged; provenance sha256 for
arc_executable_world_model.py deliberately NOT refreshed after b6787cb603 (provenance
records what produced the numbers), with a drift note explaining why no figure moves.

